zing-depression","appear_count":0,"years":[],"exams":[],"verified":false},{"id":"che-so-239","chapter_id":"chemistry-solutions","subject_id":"chemistry","stem":"A 0.050 m AlCl3 solution, taken as fully split (i = 4) in water ($K_f = 1.86$ K kg mol⁻¹), has $\\Delta T_f$ nearest","options":["0.372 K","0.093 K","1.86 K","0.744 K"],"answer_index":0,"explanation":"$\\Delta T_f = 4 \\times 1.86 \\times 0.050 = 0.372$ K.","images":[],"source":{"name":"ASTRA chemistry practice set","license":"Original syllabus-based practice questions (exam-frequent themes; not verbatim past papers)"},"difficulty":"hard","concept_id":"freezing-depression","appear_count":0,"years":[],"exams":[],"verified":false},{"id":"che-so-240","chapter_id":"chemistry-solutions","subject_id":"chemistry","stem":"Acetic acid in benzene is 60% dimerised. For a 0.20 m solution ($K_f$ of benzene = 5.12 K kg mol⁻¹), $\\Delta T_f$ is nearest","options":["0.72 K","1.02 K","0.20 K","2.56 K"],"answer_index":0,"explanation":"For dimerisation $i = 1 - \\alpha/2 = 0.70$; $\\Delta T_f = 0.70 \\times 5.12 \\times 0.20 \\approx 0.72$ K.","images":[],"source":{"name":"ASTRA chemistry practice set","license":"Original syllabus-based practice questions (exam-frequent themes; not verbatim past papers)"},"difficulty":"hard","concept_id":"freezing-depression","appear_count":0,"years":[],"exams":[],"verified":false},{"id":"che-so-241","chapter_id":"chemistry-solutions","subject_id":"chemistry","stem":"Osmosis is the spontaneous flow of solvent through a semipermeable membrane toward the","options":["more concentrated solution","less concentrated solution","vapour phase","undissolved solid solute"],"answer_index":0,"explanation":"Solvent moves to dilute the side with the higher solute concentration.","images":[],"source":{"name":"ASTRA chemistry practice set","license":"Original syllabus-based practice questions (exam-frequent themes; not verbatim past papers)"},"difficulty":"easy","concept_id":"osmotic-pressure","appear_count":